.TH SDL_DialogFileCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_DialogFileCallback \- Callback used by file dialog functions.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_dialog.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void (SDLCALL *SDL_DialogFileCallback)(void *userdata, const char * const *filelist, int filter);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The specific usage is described in each function\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR filelist
is:
.PP

\(bu NULL, an error occurred\[char46] Details can be obtained with
.BR SDL_GetError ()\[char46]
.PP
\(bu A pointer to NULL, the user either didn\(aqt choose any file or canceled the dialog\[char46]
.PP
\(bu A pointer to
.BR "" non- NULL ,
the user chose one or more files\[char46] The argument is a null-terminated array of pointers to UTF-8 encoded strings, each containing a path\[char46]
.PP
The filelist argument should not be freed; it will automatically be freed when the callback returns\[char46]
.PP
The filter argument is the index of the filter that was selected, or -1 if no filter was selected or if the platform or method doesn\(aqt support fetching the selected filter\[char46]
.PP
In Android, the
.BR filelist
are
.BR content://
URIs\[char46] They should be opened using
.BR SDL_IOFromFile ()
with appropriate modes\[char46] This applies both to open and save file dialog\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
an app-provided pointer, for the callback\(aqs use\[char46]
.TP
.I filelist
the file(s) chosen by the user\[char46]
.TP
.I filter
index of the selected filter\[char46]
.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_DialogFileFilter (3type),
.BR SDL_ShowOpenFileDialog (3),
.BR SDL_ShowSaveFileDialog (3),
.BR SDL_ShowOpenFolderDialog (3),
.BR SDL_ShowFileDialogWithProperties (3)
